# The contract between a palette and every tool that paints with one.
#
# A map inside a tool's package names one of these roles and never a colour, so a palette
# that answers every required role can be dropped in and every tool follows. A palette
# answers a role with one of its own colour names or with a rule over them, and a tool never
# learns which. The ranking words are Aura's own, its published table calls accent1 the
# Primary colour and counts up from there, and they are kept rather than replaced with
# meanings like error or success that a palette never promised.
#
# role          policy      what it is
primary         required    the accent a tool leads with
secondary       required    the second accent
tertiary        required    the third accent
quaternary      required    the fourth accent
quinary         required    the fifth accent
senary          required    the sixth accent
foreground      required    the ink
background      required    the page
comment         required    muted text that is still meant to be read
selection       required    the tint under a selected row or a selected span
highlight       required    the bar under the row a list has its cursor on, stronger than selection
subtext         required    the ink stepped back, a label on a row that is not selected
fill            required    the primary accent as a fill under a label painted in the page colour
surface         required    one step off the page, a panel or a raised row
overlay         required    secondary text, quieter than the ink and louder than a comment
dim             required    a neutral quieter than a comment, a rule or a faint label
